<div class="accordion">
<div class="accordion__item" data-toggle="false">
<a>
<i aria-hidden="true" class="fas fa-plus"></i>
              
            What Is The Recovery Time From Procedures and Treatments?</a>
<div><p>Most patients return to normal activities on the same day as their treatment. Occasionally, the area that is treated with the laser may be reddened, bruised or swollen for an hour or a few days, but camouflage cosmetics are usually able to conceal any evidence of treatment.  Typically, most treatments show little or no sign that you had anything done at all.  A mild reddening for 1-3 hours is the most common after-effect.</p>
<p>Additionally, any post-treatment discomfort can usually be relieved with extra-strength Tylenol. Your doctor may prescribe a stronger medication depending on the procedure. A topical antibiotic such as Bacitracin may also be recommended for the treatment area.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="accordion__item" data-toggle="false">
<a>
<i aria-hidden="true" class="fas fa-plus"></i>
              
            Is Laser Treatment Painful?</a>
<div><p>The sensations vary depending upon the procedure, the technology used, the wavelengths and the energy settings. Many procedures are completely painless. All are tolerable.</p>
<p>Also, most people describe the laser as feeling like the snap of a rubber band on the skin. We utilize all of the most efficient and most comfortable treatment systems including the adjustable “frozen air cooling system” that maximizes patient comfort by chilling the treatment area before, during and after the procedure.</p>
<p>In some cases, a local anesthetic may be recommended for more sensitive treatment areas or for younger patients.<br/><br/></p></div>
</div>
<div class="accordion__item" data-toggle="false">
<a>
<i aria-hidden="true" class="fas fa-plus"></i>
              
            What Conditions Can Be Treated with Cosmetic Laser Therapy?</a>
<div><p>A variety of functional and cosmetic skin problems can be treated with lasers.</p>
<p>Laser treatments can reduce the appearance of sun damage, scars, stretch marks, wrinkles, unwanted hair, fine lines, vascular lesions (birthmarks, spider veins, varicose veins and redness on the face) and uneven pigmentation.</p>
<p>Some Laser procedures include:</p>
<p><a href="https://www.shinobayderm.com/treatment/laser-resurfacing-treatments">Resurfacing Treatments</a><a href="https://www.shinobayderm.com/treatment/laser-light-therapies"></a></p>
<p><a href="https://www.shinobayderm.com/treatment/laser-light-therapies">Light Therapies</a></p>
<p><a href="https://www.shinobayderm.com/treatment/skin-tightening">Skin Tightening</a></p>
<p><a href="https://www.shinobayderm.com/treatment/fat-dissolving-reduction">Fat Dissolving &amp; Reduction</a></p></div>
</div>
<div class="accordion__item" data-toggle="false">
<a>
<i aria-hidden="true" class="fas fa-plus"></i>
              
            Do You Have Payment Plans for Cosmetic Skin Care?</a>
<div><p>Cosmetic procedures are not covered by insurance unless specified as such. All fees will be discussed with patients in advance of the procedure and are payable in advance of the procedure. We accept VISA, Discover, MasterCard, American Express and Debit Cards.<br/><br/>For cosmetic packages and procedures we offer financing options for 6-18 months and other financing options featuring low interest for up to 60 months through our credit providers Alphaeon Credit and CareCredit (with approved credit).<br/><br/>You can be approved within a few minutes while you are at your appointment.<br/><br/>For further information regarding our payment policies or pre-approval on credit amounts please contact our office directly at <a href="tel:954-765-3005" rel="noopener">954-765-3005</a>. We will do our best to find you a plan that works with your budget.</p></div>
